  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isoamyl isothiocyanate may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of intermediate targets. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where Isoamyl isothiocyanate acts as a target for different enzymes, which in turn target Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. Specifically, the compound is linked to Methionine aminopeptidase 2 and Ovalicin, both of which are known to target Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. Additionally, Isoamyl isothiocyanate is also linked to Acyl-CoA hydrolase, which is further connected to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. These findings collectively imply that Isoamyl isothiocyanate may exert its biological effects through a cascade of enzymatic interactions, ultimately influencing Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The evidence is consistent across different scoring metrics, suggesting a plausible and well-supported relationship. However, the exact mechanism by which Isoamyl isothiocyanate influences the downstream targets remains to be fully elucidated.",
